§§ `Part 2 Division 5 -- offences`

-- Arguments: holder, volunteer, s 28/29 duty, owed, breached, exposed, no excuse, great shortfall, high risk, merits
-- punishment, aware of substantial risk, unjustifiable, died, contributed.
-- Gross negligence (s 4(2)) and a death: industrial manslaughter by a body corporate.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)`
-- Recklessness (s 4(3)) and a death: industrial manslaughter by the individual running the business.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `industrial manslaughter (s 30A)`
-- The shortfall and the risk, but not so as to merit criminal punishment, and not reckless: Category 2.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
-- Aware of the risk but taking it was not unjustifiable: not reckless; Category 2.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
-- Gross negligence and a death the conduct did not substantially contribute to: Category 1.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
-- Gross negligence but a reasonable excuse, no death: Category 2.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
-- A worker grossly negligent, causing a death: not industrial manslaughter (s 30A names only the business and its officers).
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `another individual, such as a worker or other person at the workplace` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `a Category 1 offence (s 31)`
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a Category 3 offence (s 33)`
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `a body corporate conducting the business or undertaking` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`
-- s 34(2): a volunteer officer, not a worker's duty; a volunteer with a worker's duty.
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `an individual conducting the business or undertaking, or an officer of it` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `another individual, such as a worker or other person at the workplace` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `a Category 2 offence (s 32)`
-- s 34(3).
#ASSERT `Which offence do these facts make out` `an unincorporated association` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no offence under Part 2 on these facts`

